From 3805a6c4e003d4efb98446cdcb1e20e64acc1e2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 21:39:29 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] test(3d): pin the as-imported sample's 3D Pocket refusal
 (#1706)

The heavy-lane test the_sample_as_imported_still_generates_both_operations
asked a 6 mm 3D Pocket to cut the as-imported sample_ap214. The part casts
a strip only 6.53 mm wide from above, and the 3D Pocket machine area is
the model's own silhouette, so no level has room for the tool. The ladder
refuses with "nothing to cut: the model fills the pocket at every level".
The refusal is correct. The test failed from its first commit (6726c1b81,
PR #1419); it is ignored, so the v0.20.0 gate was its first run.

The heavy test now generates and verifies the 3D Finish S1 alone. A new
default test pins the R1 refusal by its text. No product code changes.

Fixes #1706

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
